A||||2||V8Fiero||Checking starter off of car??||||1||
Z||000000||V8Fiero||01-20-2001||02:59 PM||||Just wondering how to see if a starter is good before I put it on my car. Mine went out and I have one from a parts car and dont want to take the time to put it on if it doesnt work.....<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||862M4inCA||01-20-2001||03:37 PM||||Well, you have a few options. I know that if you have an Autozone store near you they can test it on a bench, otherwise what I've been known to do (when I need to know quick) is to grab some jumper cables, attach them to a battery and connect the negative to the starter body, positive to where the positive wire normally goes, and then grab a wire with aligator clips on either end and attach it to the positive cable and then holding the starter firmly (to prevent movement from torque) touch the smaller post on the solenoid. If the starter is good it should spin up, otherwise find another. Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Fiero||01-20-2001||08:38 PM||||Hey thanks for the tip. I had tried it earlier with the jumper cables but didnt ground the body of the starter. I tested it and it worked great and now my daily driver is back on the road. Thanks a million.....<BR>fieros rule!!!!||||reg||1
